abour very well… I haven’t done any perineal massages, and am now worrying because I also haven’t had sex since we conceived. I’ve always found things painful down there - sex used to be so painful it was impossible, and things like smears I</div><div class="timestamp finePrint">a day ago by Mama1to3</div><div class="postActions mui-1u45zpb"><div class="mui-1u45zpb"><div class="leftSideCmntCount finePrint "><svg class="MuiSvgIcon-root MuiSvgIcon-fontSizeMedium commentIcon mui-q7mezt" focusable="false" role="img" viewBox="0 0 24 24" style="color:#C2C2BC" aria-label="Number of comments"><path d="M20 4v12H5.17L4 17.17V4zm0-2H4c-1.1 0-2 .9-2 2v15.59c0 .89 1.08 1.34 1.71.71L6 18h14c1.1 0 2-.9 2-2V4c0-1.1-.9-2-2-2"></path><title>Number of comments</title></svg><span>1</span></div><div class="leftSideReactions"><div class="mui-lycs4w"><div class="emojisWrapper mui-1f3bocu"><img src="https://assets.babycenter.com/ims/2023/12/ic_heart_gray_rejuv.svg" alt="no reactions" width="18" height="18"/></div><div class="count">0</div></div></div></div></div></div></li><li id="post-34142294" class=""><a class="mui-12mmxgd" href="/groups/a225/pregnancy">Pregnancy</a><div class="hoverTextOnly mui-8an92f"><div class="titleText"><a class="hoverText" href="/post/a34142294/aspirin-in-pregnancy-helppppp-please">Aspirin in pregnancy helppppp please </a></div><div><div class="mui-1veg32a"><div class="postAvatar"><div class="containsLetter mui-a7usph" size="20" aria-hidden="true">a</div></div><span class="nameAndGroup finePrint">By ANXIOUSANNIE </span></div></div><div class="postBody bodyLinks">I’m currently 12 weeks pregnant, yet to have my scan which is due shortly, I had a reassurance scan at 8 weeks and all was well thankfully, however I have been recommended to start aspirin, but nobody seems to be able to reassure me or give me the information I’ve been looking for aside from studies</div><div class="timestamp finePrint">a day ago by Mama1to3</div><div class="postActions mui-1u45zpb"><div class="mui-1u45zpb"><div class="leftSideCmntCount finePrint "><svg class="MuiSvgIcon-root MuiSvgIcon-fontSizeMedium commentIcon mui-q7mezt" focusable="false" role="img" viewBox="0 0 24 24" style="color:#C2C2BC" aria-label="Number of comments"><path d="M20 4v12H5.17L4 17.17V4zm0-2H4c-1.1 0-2 .9-2 2v15.59c0 .89 1.08 1.34 1.71.71L6 18h14c1.1 0 2-.9 2-2V4c0-1.1-.9-2-2-2"></path><title>Number of comments</title></svg><span>4</span></div><div class="leftSideReactions"><div class="mui-lycs4w"><div class="emojisWrapper mui-1f3bocu"><img src="https://assets.babycenter.com/ims/2023/12/ic_heart_gray_rejuv.svg" alt="no reactions" width="18" height="18"/></div><div class="count">0</div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="adUnitWrapper"><div class="greyAdBox mui-1qwcnd7"><div class="advertisementLabel grey">Advertisement | page continues below</div><div class="adSlotContainer grey"><ad-container id="medRectMobWrapper" style="display:block"><div id="medRectMob" class="adBox" style="text-align:center"></div></ad-container></div></div></div></li><li id="post-34142218" class=""><a class="mui-12mmxgd" href="/groups/a225/pregnancy">Pregnancy</a><div class="hoverTextOnly mui-8an92f"><div class="titleText"><a class="hoverText" href="/post/a34142218/induction-and-epidural">Induction and epidural</a></div><div><div class="mui-1veg32a"><div class="postAvatar"><div class="containsLetter mui-nkvp61" size="20" aria-hidden="true">c</div></div><span class="nameAndGroup finePrint">By Cmj2908 </span></div></div><div class="postBody bodyLinks">Hi Ladies,
My waters broke at 34 +4, so I'm being induced at 37 weeks. The plan initially was cesarean, but due to baby safety, it's been agreed vaginal is safer. 
I've asked for an epidural before the drip as I've heard horror stories about contractions when using the drip. 
However im terrified th</div><div class="timestamp finePrint">13-10-26 by craig15miller</div><div class="postActions mui-1u45zpb"><div class="mui-1u45zpb"><div class="leftSideCmntCount finePrint "><svg class="MuiSvgIcon-root MuiSvgIcon-fontSizeMedium commentIcon mui-q7mezt" focusable="false" role="img" viewBox="0 0 24 24" style="color:#C2C2BC" aria-label="Number of comments"><path d="M20 4v12H5.17L4 17.17V4zm0-2H4c-1.1 0-2 .9-2 2v15.59c0 .89 1.08 1.34 1.71.71L6 18h14c1.1 0 2-.9 2-2V4c0-1.1-.9-2-2-2"></path><title>Number of comments</title></svg><span>1</span></div><div class="leftSideReactions"><div class="mui-lycs4w"><div class="emojisWrapper mui-1f3bocu"><img src="https://assets.babycenter.com/ims/2023/12/ic_heart_gray_rejuv.svg" alt="no reactions" width="18" height="18"/></div><div class="count">0</div></div></div></div></div></div></li><li id="post-34142204" class=""><a class="mui-12mmxgd" href="/groups/a225/pregnancy">Pregnancy</a><div class="hoverTextOnly mui-8an92f"><div class="titleText"><a class="hoverText" href="/post/a34142204/baby-kicks-how-do-you-feel-them">Baby &quot;kicks&quot;. How do you feel them?</a></div><div><div class="mui-1veg32a"><div class="postAvatar"><div class="containsLetter mui-1xpclmf" size="20" aria-hidden="true">s</div></div><span class="nameAndGroup finePrint">By SnoopyMummy </span></div></div><div class="postBody bodyLinks">I am pregnant for the 1st time, week 21 now.

I'm so confused about what exactly to call a baby kick/movement. 
Last week's scan I was told I have anterior placenta.

I feel things but slight and not very frequent.
I'm not able to tell if the feeling is the baby "kicks" or my body's normal responses</div><div class="timestamp finePrint">a day ago by Mama1to3</div><div class="postActions mui-1u45zpb"><div class="mui-1u45zpb"><div class="leftSideCmntCount finePrint "><svg class="MuiSvgIcon-root MuiSvgIcon-fontSizeMedium commentIcon mui-q7mezt" focusable="false" role="img" viewBox="0 0 24 24" style="color:#C2C2BC" aria-label="Number of comments"><path d="M20 4v12H5.17L4 17.17V4zm0-2H4c-1.1 0-2 .9-2 2v15.59c0 .89 1.08 1.34 1.71.71L6 18h14c1.1 0 2-.9 2-2V4c0-1.1-.9-2-2-2"></path><title>Number of comments</title></svg><span>5</span></div><div class="leftSideReactions"><div class="mui-lycs4w"><div class="emojisWrapper mui-1f3bocu"><img src="https://assets.babycenter.com/ims/2023/12/ic_heart_gray_rejuv.svg" alt="no reactions" width="18" height="18"/></div><div class="count">0</div></div></div></div></div></div></li><li id="post-34142184" class=""><a class="mui-12mmxgd" href="/groups/a225/pregnancy">Pregnancy</a><div class="hoverTextOnly mui-8an92f"><div class="titleText"><a class="hoverText" href="/post/a34142184/short-cervix">short cervix </a></div><div><div class="mui-1veg32a"><div class="postAvatar"><div class="containsLetter mui-tm69gb" size="20" aria-hidden="true">g</div></div><span class="nameAndGroup finePrint">By gari2 </span></div></div><div class="postBody bodyLinks">hey everyone i hope you all are fine and healthy this is my second pregnancy..in first i had a miscarriage around 4.5 month due to short cervix last year and by then this month i conceived it is my 6th week my doctor advised me to take bed rest but from today i noticed some old brown tissue while ur</div><div class="timestamp finePrint">12-10-26 by LyndaBC</div><div class="postActions mui-1u45zpb"><div class="mui-1u45zpb"><div class="leftSideCmntCount finePrint "><svg class="MuiSvgIcon-root MuiSvgIcon-fontSizeMedium commentIcon mui-q7mezt" focusable="false" role="img" viewBox="0 0 24 24" style="color:#C2C2BC" aria-label="Number of comments"><path d="M20 4v12H5.17L4 17.17V4zm0-2H4c-1.1 0-2 .9-2 2v15.59c0 .89 1.08 1.34 1.71.71L6 18h14c1.1 0 2-.9 2-2V4c0-1.1-.9-2-2-2"></path><title>Number of comments</title></svg><span>1</span></div><div class="leftSideReactions"><div class="mui-lycs4w"><div class="emojisWrapper mui-1f3bocu"><img src="https://assets.babycenter.com/ims/2023/12/ic_heart_gray_rejuv.svg" alt="no reactions" width="18" height="18"/></div><div class="count">0</div></div></div></div></div></div></li></ul><div class="seeMoreWrapper"><a class="MuiButtonBase-root MuiButton-root MuiButton-text MuiButton-textPrimary MuiButton-sizeMedium MuiButton-textSizeMedium MuiButton-colorPrimary MuiButton-root MuiButton-text MuiButton-textPrimary MuiButton-sizeMedium MuiButton-textSizeMedium MuiButton-colorPrimary whiteBtn mui-x5juai" tabindex="0" href="/groups/topic/3/pregnancy">See more</a></div></section><section class="mui-i7uzrb"><h2>Posts about babies</h2><ul class="postList unstyledLinks communityText mui-1sh4vf"><li id="post-34142505" class=""><a class="mui-12mmxgd" href="/groups/a2975/breastfeeding">Breastfeeding</a><div class="hoverTextOnly mui-8an92f"><div class="titleText"><a class="hoverText" href="/post/a34142505/nursing-strike-mastitis-drop-in-supply">Nursing strike, Mastitis &amp; drop in supply </a></div><div><div class="mui-1veg32a"><div class="postAvatar"><div class="containsLetter mui-1fi14tk" size="20" aria-hidden="true">d</div></div><span class="nameAndGroup finePrint">By DaniellaLo </span></div></div><div class="postBody bodyLinks">Hello,

I’m here looking for help/ experiences and maybe also just a good vent.

My baby and I had a bit of a rough start to breastfeeding. The end of her birth ended in a forceps delivery (nearly an emergency c section that would have had me put under). She was then in NICU and I put under for stit</div><div class="timestamp finePrint">23-10-26 </div><div class="postActions mui-1u45zpb"><div class="mui-1u45zpb"><div class="leftSideCmntCount finePrint "><svg class="MuiSvgIcon-root MuiSvgIcon-fontSizeMedium commentIcon mui-q7mezt" focusable="false" role="img" viewBox="0 0 24 24" style="color:#C2C2BC" aria-label="Number of comments"><path d="M20 4v12H5.17L4 17.17V4zm0-2H4c-1.1 0-2 .9-2 2v15.59c0 .89 1.08 1.34 1.71.71L6 18h14c1.1 0 2-.9 2-2V4c0-1.1-.9-2-2-2"></path><title>Number of comments</title></svg><span>0</span></div><div class="leftSideReactions"><div class="mui-lycs4w"><div class="emojisWrapper mui-1f3bocu"><img src="https://assets.babycenter.com/ims/2023/12/ic_heart_gray_rejuv.svg" alt="no reactions" width="18" height="18"/></div><div class="count">0</div></div></div></div></div></div></li><li id="post-34142498" class=""><a class="mui-12mmxgd" href="/groups/a712475/whats_your_opinion_on">What&#x27;s Your Opinion On ...?</a><div class="hoverTextOnly mui-8an92f"><div class="titleText"><a class="hoverText" href="/post/a34142498/is-the-museum-right">Is the museum right?</a></div><div><div class="mui-1veg32a"><div class="postAvatar"><div class="mui-1xpclmf" size="20" aria-hidden="true"><img src="https://static.babycenter.com/user/wiWEFRt6LAvPLk61/939245c0-2c57-4d68-996f-3eb855466e65_w80.gif" alt="member avatar" width="20" height="20" loading="lazy"/></div></div><span class="nameAndGroup finePrint">By Snow27 </span></div></div><div class="postBody bodyLinks">A Scottish museum has removed its Egyptian mummy from its display as a mark of respect.

A Glasgow life spokesman said: 

“The removal of human remains from display at Glasgow Life museums reflects contemporary museum practice.

“The International Council of Museums’ revised code of ethics, publishe</div><div class="timestamp finePrint">18 hours ago by MrDude</div><div class="postActions mui-1u45zpb"><div class="mui-1u45zpb"><div class="leftSideCmntCount finePrint "><svg class="MuiSvgIcon-root MuiSvgIcon-fontSizeMedium commentIcon mui-q7mezt" focusable="false" role="img" viewBox="0 0 24 24" style="color:#C2C2BC" aria-label="Number of comments"><path d="M20 4v12H5.17L4 17.17V4zm0-2H4c-1.1 0-2 .9-2 2v15.59c0 .89 1.08 1.34 1.71.71L6 18h14c1.1 0 2-.9 2-2V4c0-1.1-.9-2-2-2"></path><title>Number of comments</title></svg><span>7</span></div><div class="leftSideReactions"><div class="mui-lycs4w"><div class="emojisWrapper mui-1f3bocu"><img src="https://assets.babycenter.com/ims/2023/12/ic_heart_gray_rejuv.svg" alt="no reactions" width="18" height="18"/></div><div class="count">0</div></div></div></div></div></div></li><li id="post-34142485" class=""><a class="mui-12mmxgd" href="/groups/a712475/whats_your_opinion_on">What&#x27;s Your Opinion On ...?</a><div class="hoverTextOnly mui-8an92f"><div class="titleText"><a class="hoverText" href="/post/a34142485/stay-or-drop-off-parties-does-it-matter">Stay or drop off (parties) does it matter?</a></div><div><div class="mui-1veg32a"><div class="postAvatar"><div class="mui-1xpclmf" size="20" aria-hidden="true"><img src="https://static.babycenter.com/user/wiWEFRt6LAvPLk61/939245c0-2c57-4d68-996f-3eb855466e65_w80.gif" alt="member avatar" width="20" height="20" loading="lazy"/></div></div><span class="nameAndGroup finePrint">By Snow27 </span></div></div><div class="postBody bodyLinks">Just seen an interesting debate online, regarding a childs birthday party (7) and a parent wanting to stay. The host stated that no adult can stay.

I've just been to an 8 year olds party last week, where all (apart from 1) parents stayed. Most parents we know will not drop off and leave, including </div><div class="timestamp finePrint">a day ago by Sophie19842</div><div class="postActions mui-1u45zpb"><div class="mui-1u45zpb"><div class="leftSideCmntCount finePrint "><svg class="MuiSvgIcon-root MuiSvgIcon-fontSizeMedium commentIcon mui-q7mezt" focusable="false" role="img" viewBox="0 0 24 24" style="color:#C2C2BC" aria-label="Number of comments"><path d="M20 4v12H5.17L4 17.17V4zm0-2H4c-1.1 0-2 .9-2 2v15.59c0 .89 1.08 1.34 1.71.71L6 18h14c1.1 0 2-.9 2-2V4c0-1.1-.9-2-2-2"></path><title>Number of comments</title></svg><span>15</span></div><div class="leftSideReactions"><div class="mui-lycs4w"><div class="emojisWrapper mui-1f3bocu"><img src="https://assets.babycenter.com/ims/2023/12/ic_heart_gray_rejuv.svg" alt="no reactions" width="18" height="18"/></div><div class="count">0</div></div></div></div></div></div></li><li id="post-34142465" class=""><a class="mui-12mmxgd" href="/groups/a235/baby">Baby</a><div class="hoverTextOnly mui-8an92f"><div class="titleText"><a class="hoverText" href="/post/a34142465/diarrhea">Diarrhea </a></div><div><div class="mui-1veg32a"><div class="postAvatar"><div class="containsLetter mui-n97xdp" size="20" aria-hidden="true">h</div></div><span class="nameAndGroup finePrint">By Heenameenadika </span></div></div><div class="postBody bodyLinks">My baby boy 15days old suffering from vomiting n loose motion what to do? </div><div class="timestamp finePrint">22-10-26 </div><div class="postActions mui-1u45zpb"><div class="mui-1u45zpb"><div class="leftSideCmntCount finePrint "><svg class="MuiSvgIcon-root MuiSvgIcon-fontSizeMedium commentIcon mui-q7mezt" focusable="false" role="img" viewBox="0 0 24 24" style="color:#C2C2BC" aria-label="Number of comments"><path d="M20 4v12H5.17L4 17.17V4zm0-2H4c-1.1 0-2 .9-2 2v15.59c0 .89 1.08 1.34 1.71.71L6 18h14c1.1 0 2-.9 2-2V4c0-1.1-.9-2-2-2"></path><title>Number of comments</title></svg><span>0</span></div><div class="leftSideReactions"><div class="mui-lycs4w"><div class="emojisWrapper mui-1f3bocu"><img src="https://assets.babycenter.com/ims/2023/12/ic_heart_gray_rejuv.svg" alt="no reactions" width="18" height="18"/></div><div class="count">0</div></div></div></div></div></div></li><li id="post-34142464" class=""><a class="mui-12mmxgd" href="/groups/a712475/whats_your_opinion_on">What&#x27;s Your Opinion On ...?</a><div class="hoverTextOnly mui-8an92f"><div class="titleText"><a class="hoverText" href="/post/a34142464/how-long-does-a-coffee-buy-you-a-seat-for">How long does a coffee buy you a seat for?</a></div><div><div class="mui-1veg32a"><div class="postAvatar"><div class="mui-1xpclmf" size="20" aria-hidden="true"><img src="https://imageserve.babycenter.com/16/000/433/fZqVMcaKTyvFZ5QvH2prk90kqiEbNUkY_sq.jpg" alt="member avatar" width="20" height="20" loading="lazy"/></div></div><span class="nameAndGroup finePrint">By SmokeMeAKipper </span></div></div><div class="postBody bodyLinks">In a coffee shop how long do you think it's reasonable to sit in a coffee shop?  Is it rude to overstay your welcome in such an establishment if you've bought something? 

Does buying more entitle you to stay longer even after you've finished eating/drinking?

